    "memoText": "\n \n                         VETO MESSAGE - No. 261\n \nTO THE SENATE:\n \nI am returning herewith, without my approval, the following bill:\n \nSenate Bill Number 3291, entitled:\n \n    \"AN ACT to amend the elder law, in relation to creating and distrib-\n      uting a drug guide for senior consumers\"\n \n    NOT APPROVED\n \n  This bill would require the New York State Office for the Aging (NYSO-\nFA),  in  conjunction with the State Board of Pharmacy, and in consulta-\ntion with the New York State Department of Health, to  prepare,  publish\nand  update  a  Senior Drug Guide in order to explain the use, function,\nand common drug interactions of drugs commonly used by persons over  the\nage  of  sixty-two.  This  guide  would  also be required to include the\neffects of combining such medications with alcohol consumption.\n\n  While the intent of this bill is laudable, developing, providing,  and\nmaintaining  up to date information to the public regarding the composi-\ntion of medications and their potential side effects,  including  inter-\nactions  that could occur when medications are mixed with other types of\ndrugs such as alcohol, is beyond NYSOFA's scope of practice  and  exper-\ntise. Providing information and assistance about medications, medication\nsafety,  medication  side effects and drug interactions falls within the\nrealm of the practice of licensed pharmacy  and  medical  professionals.\nFor these reasons I am constrained to disapprove this bill.\n \n  The bill is disapproved.                    (signed) ANDREW M. CUOMO\n \n                               __________\n",
